+| Progression payoff | 9/10 | Chapter 8, Lira using the slow left as a visible feint; Chapter 9, Cael choosing the ground-read over Pressure, Anchor, and Wind | Capability changes consequence while limits remain active. The most satisfying progress is judgment: both characters use less power, more precisely. | High |
+| Connection | 9/10 | Chapter 7's forty-first notch and delayed ruling; Chapter 9's forty-seventh notch and first boat; Chapter 12's wand laid beside the report | The movement is tightly braided. The boat, bag, cloth, boxes, hands, wounds, count, and town all move from plant to payoff or charged continuation. | High |
+| Read-aloud quality | 9/10 | Chapter 9, "He did not haul" through "he gave it nowhere to go"; Chapter 12, the stick ascending the stairs | Repetition, sentence weight, and sound cues produce excellent oral rhythm. Dense administrative explanations are the main exception, not the prevailing texture. | High |
+
+For this lens, the movement's major strength is the equivalence it builds among physical and moral structures: a post needs a sound footing, a claim needs a source, a gift needs a receipt, and a person without office still has to decide what will bear weight.
